ct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and June to July came in under 90% of normal in 42 of those 75 years. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, June to July hit 148% and November to December fell to 28%. So far in 2026, June to July stands at 168%. On grid 11829, a preliminary estimate puts August to September 2026 at 22.3, and that estimate can change.</p>"}
